able>caption{display:table-caption!important}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table>tbody{display:table-row-group}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table th,body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table td{padding-left:inherit;padding-right:inherit}}</style><table class=\"infobox biography vcard\"><tbody><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-above\"><div class=\"fn\">Yukihiro Matsumoto</div></th></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\" style=\"font-size: 125%\"><span title=\"Japanese-language text\"><span lang=\"ja-Hira\">まつもと ゆきひろ</span></span>&#160;<span class=\"languageicon\" style=\"font-size:100%; font-weight:normal\">(<a href=\"/wiki/Japanese_language\" title=\"Japanese language\">Japanese</a>)</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Yukihiro_Matsumoto_(2018).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Yukihiro_Matsumoto_%282018%29.jpg/250px-Yukihiro_Matsumoto_%282018%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"304\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Yukihiro_Matsumoto_%282018%29.jpg/500px-Yukihiro_Matsumoto_%282018%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3279\" data-file-height=\"3984\" /></a></span><div class=\"infobox-caption\">Yukihiro Matsumoto in 2018</div></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Born</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><span style=\"display:none\"> (<span class=\"bday\">1965-04-14</span>) </span>14 April 1965<span class=\"noprint ForceAgeToShow\"> (age&#160;61)</span><br /><div style=\"display:inline\" class=\"birthplace\"><a href=\"/wiki/Osaka_Prefecture\" title=\"Osaka Prefecture\">Osaka Prefecture</a>, Japan</div><span style=\"display:none\" data-plural=\"1\"></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Other&#160;name</th><td class=\"infobox-data nickname\">Matz</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Education</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><a href=\"/wiki/University_of_Tsukuba\" title=\"University of Tsukuba\">University of Tsukuba</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/Bachelor_of_Science\" title=\"Bachelor of Science\">BS</a>)<br /><a href=\"/wiki/Shimane_University\" title=\"Shimane University\">Shimane University</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Occupations</th><td class=\"infobox-data role\">Computer scientist, programmer, author</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Known&#160;for</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ruby_(programming_language)\" title=\"Ruby (programming language)\">Ruby</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Children</th><td class=\"infobox-data\">4</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Yukihiro_Matsumoto_EuRuKo_2011.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Yukihiro_Matsumoto_EuRuKo_2011.jpg/250px-Yukihiro_Matsumoto_EuRuKo_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"241\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Yukihiro_Matsumoto_EuRuKo_2011.jpg/500px-Yukihiro_Matsumoto_EuRuKo_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2885\" data-file-height=\"2784\" /></a><figcaption>Matsumoto giving the keynote speech at EuRuKo 2011</figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Matz.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Matz.jpg/250px-Matz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"321\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Matz.jpg/500px-Matz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1893\" data-file-height=\"2430\" /></a><figcaption>Matsumoto accepting an award from the <a href=\"/wiki/Free_Software_Foundation\" title=\"Free Software Foundation\">Free Software Foundation</a> (founder <a href=\"/wiki/Richard_Stallman\" title=\"Richard Stallman\">Richard Stallman</a>, right) in 2012</figcaption></figure>\n<p><b>Yukihiro Matsumoto</b><span style=\"font-weight: normal\"> (<span title=\"Japanese-language text\"><span lang=\"ja\">まつもとゆきひろ</span></span>, <span title=\"Hepburn transliteration\"><i lang=\"ja-Latn\">Matsumoto Yukihiro</i></span>; born 14 April 1965)</span>, also known as <b>Matz</b>, is a Japanese computer scientist and <a href=\"/wiki/Software_programmer\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Software programmer\">software programmer</a>. He is best known as the chief designer of the <a href=\"/wiki/Ruby_(programming_language)\" title=\"Ruby (programming language)\">Ruby</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Programming_language\" title=\"Programming language\">programming language</a> and its original reference implementation, <a href=\"/wiki/Matz%27s_Ruby_Interpreter\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Matz&#39;s Ruby Interpreter\">Matz's Ruby Interpreter</a> (MRI).\n</p><p>As of 2011<sup class=\"plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update\" style=\"display:none;\"><a class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Yukihiro_Matsumoto&amp;action=edit\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Yukihiro_Matsumoto&amp;action=edit\">&#91;update&#93;</a></sup>, Matsumoto is the Chief Architect of Ruby at <a href=\"/wiki/Heroku\" title=\"Heroku\">Heroku</a>, an online cloud <a href=\"/wiki/Platform-as-a-service\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Platform-as-a-service\">platform-as-a-service</a> in San Francisco.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">&#91;<i><a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Dates_and_numbers#Chronological_items\" title=\"Wikipedia:Manual of Style/Dates and numbers\"><span title=\"This information is in need of an update. (August 2025)\">needs update</span></a></i>&#93;</sup> He is a fellow of the <a href=\"/wiki/Rakuten_Institute_of_Technology\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rakuten Institute of Technology\">Rakuten Institute of Technology</a>, a research and development organization within <a href=\"/wiki/Rakuten\" title=\"Rakuten\">Rakuten Group, Inc.</a> He was appointed to the role of technical advisor for VASILY, Inc. starting in June 2014.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1333433106\">.mw-parser-output cite.citation{font-style:inherit;word-wrap:break-word}.mw-parser-output .citation q{quotes:\"\\\"\"\"\\\"\"\"'\"\"'\"}.mw-parser-output .citation:target{background-color:rgba(0,127,255,0.133)}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-free.id-lock-free a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Lock-green.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited.id-lock-limited a,.mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration.id-lock-registration a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Lock-gray-alt-2.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription.id-lock